# ============================================================
# OWLI — ROOT .HTACCESS (server-level protection)
#
# PURPOSE: The GitHub deployment publishes the whole repository
# into public_html/ — including project docs. Those files are NOT
# meant for the web: GO-LIVE-STEPS.md once listed every coupon
# code (anyone could read them at /GO-LIVE-STEPS.md). This file
# makes Apache refuse them BEFORE PHP or static serving runs.
#
# WHAT IS BLOCKED (403):
#   *.md   — README.md, CLAUDE.md, GO-LIVE-STEPS.md, PRD.md, prompt.md
#   *.sql  — sql/schema.sql (also blocked by sql/.htaccess)
#   *.log  — any stray log file
#   *.ini  — any stray config file
#
# NOTES:
#   - Hostinger's Apache honours .htaccess (verified live: api/.htaccess
#     answers 403 before PHP runs).
#   - The local Docker Apache also honours it (AllowOverride All for the
#     docroot), so localhost:8800 behaves the same way.
#   - scripts/ has its own stricter .htaccess (everything denied) —
#     validate.php is a CLI tool, not a web page.
#   - Nothing public references any blocked file, so no page breaks.
# ============================================================

<FilesMatch "\.(md|sql|log|ini)$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>
